## Privacy Policy

**Effective date:** [effective date]

[Developer/company name] ("we", "us") operates the mobile game **Bloom**
(the "App"). This policy explains what data the App collects, why, and
what choices you have.

### 1. Data we collect

**We do not collect your name, email, phone number, or any other
directly-identifying information.** The App has no account system and no
login.

| Data | Purpose | Collected by |
|---|---|---|
| App usage events (upgrade purchases, specimen shares, tree presses, IAP purchases, settings changes) | Understand which parts of the game are used, tune balance | Firebase Analytics (Google) |
| Crash reports and error logs | Fix bugs | Firebase Crashlytics (Google) |
| Advertising identifier (IDFA on iOS, Android Advertising ID on Android) and other device/ad-interaction data | Show ads (double-harvest, growth boost, instant-fill, mutation/seed bonuses, streak restore, interstitial), measure ad performance; may be used by our ad partner for personalized advertising if you allow tracking | Google AdMob, and AdMob's own mediated ad networks |
| Purchase receipts | Process "Remove Ads" and "Eternal Sun" purchases and let you restore them on a new device | Apple App Store / Google Play billing |

_If a new third-party service is ever added, add a row here. See §0.1
above for which of these are live vs. still test-only/pending as of this
writing._

### 2. Data stored only on your device

Your sap/seed totals, tree upgrade levels, unlocked mutations, permanent
specimen collection, offline-harvest and boost usage counters, check-in
streak, and sound settings are stored locally on your device only. This
data is not sent to us and is deleted if you uninstall the App. There is
currently no cloud save or cross-device sync.

### 3. Advertising and tracking

The App shows ads (an interstitial when leaving a secondary screen, an
app-open ad, and several optional "watch a video" ads you choose to view
in exchange for a doubled offline harvest, a temporary growth boost,
instant-filled biomass, a bonus mutation/seed option, or a restored
check-in streak) served through **Google AdMob**. AdMob may work with
third-party ad networks that set their own cookies or device identifiers.

**On iOS**, the App is required to show Apple's App Tracking Transparency
prompt before using the advertising identifier for personalized ads. The
App asks once, the first time you open it. If you decline, you'll still see
ads, just not ones personalized to your interests; you can change your
answer at any time in iOS Settings → Privacy & Security → Tracking.

**On Android**, ads may use the Android Advertising ID unless you've
opted out of ad personalization in your device's Google Settings.

You can review Google's own privacy practices for AdMob at
https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads.

### 4. In-app purchases

The App offers two purchases: "Remove Ads" (removes interstitial, banner,
and app-open ads; harvest stays permanently doubled) and "Eternal Sun"
(immediately maxes offline production rate and reservoir cap). Payment is
processed entirely by Apple or Google — we never see or store your
payment card details.

### 5. Children's privacy

The App is a general-audience casual idle game and is not directed at
children under 13 (or the relevant age of consent in your country). We do
not knowingly collect personal information from children. [If you intend
to market this app toward children, or expect a substantial child
audience, you must revisit this section together with Google Play's
Families Policy and the FTC's COPPA rule — that changes what ad
personalization and analytics are allowed and is out of scope of this
draft.]

### 6. Data retention and deletion

Analytics and crash data are retained by Firebase per Google's standard
retention settings. Since the App has no account system, there's no
"delete my account" action — uninstalling the App removes all
locally-stored data, and you can request deletion of any analytics data
tied to your device by contacting us at [support email] with your
device's advertising identifier.

### 7. Your choices

- **Ad personalization**: controlled by your OS-level setting (iOS App
  Tracking Transparency; Android "Opt out of Ads
  Personalization").
- **Remove ads entirely**: the in-app "Remove Ads" purchase removes the
  interstitial, banner, and app-open ads (rewarded video, which you opt
  into per-use for a bonus, stays available since it's your choice, not an
  interruption).

### 8. Changes to this policy

We may update this policy as the App changes. Material changes will be
reflected by updating the effective date above.

